{
  "analysis": "The gated candidate completed successfully and achieved validation HR@10 of 0.605, improving on 0.600 by 0.005 absolute (0.5 percentage points). This falls below the proposed 0.010–0.020 gain. The best checkpoint occurred at epoch 5 of 25 completed epochs. Results support retaining the lightweight scale gate for further comparison, but one seeded run does not establish statistical significance or prove that adaptive scale selection caused the improvement.",
  "code_summary": "One causal, position-free NextItNet with 64-dimensional tied item embeddings and eight independent residual blocks using dilations [1,2,4,8,1,2,4,8]. Each block combines width-3 local and dilated convolutions through a channel-wise sigmoid gate computed by a pointwise convolution. Zero-initialized gate weights and biases give g=0.5 initially, preserving the previous fusion (local+dilated)/sqrt(2). Layer normalization, GELU, dropout, a second dilated convolution, residual connections, padding masks, last-nonpadding selection, and tied-embedding dot-product scoring remain intact. Constants remain MAXLEN=128, HIDDEN_UNITS=64, NUM_BLOCKS=8, KERNEL_SIZE=3, DROPOUT_RATE=0.2, LR=0.001, WEIGHT_DECAY=0.0, BATCH_SIZE=128; training and evaluation remain host-owned."
}
